  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Pure Gold**: rare: 10 archived performances [2]\n- **Song for Mark & Joel**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [2]\n- **Love Love Love | First Attempt**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **John Banters About His Hair**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Going to Monaco**: back after 98 archived shows (2679 days); rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n- **Genesis 30&3**: back after 41 archived shows (1281 days); rare: 11 archived performances [2]\n- **Enoch 18&14**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Absolute Lithops Effect**: rare: 9 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2013-10-13** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 86 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Enoch 18&14 |, Ezekiel 7 and the Permanent Efficacy of Grace |, Genesis 30&3 |, The Diaz Brothers |, Woke Up New | [1]\n- John and Peter performed as a duo, with John adding solo songs mid-set [1]\n- The uploader described the venue as unusually beautiful and impeccable [1]\n- The Dutch crowd was noted as being extremely polite and quiet [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2013-10-13**: taped by ∂®∑@Mßøä†; source: iPhone [1]",
